{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg9xGNXzqykPmRioKdsJC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The recovery middleware now treats a `panic(http.ErrAbortHandler)` like a broken pipe. It no longer logs the \"panic recovered\" stack trace or replaces the response with a 500. It logs one short line, records the error on the context, and aborts. The recovery and panic tests pass, and `go vet` and `gofmt` are clean. I didn't run the full test suite.\n\n**The change, in `recovery.go`:** the check for whether a panic is a broken pipe now also matches `http.ErrAbortHandler`:\n```go\nif e, ok := err.(error); ok && errors.Is(e, http.ErrAbortHandler) {\n\tbrokenPipe = true\n}\n```\n`net/http` itself skips the stack trace for this value, because handlers raise it on purpose to abort a response. `errors.Is` also catches errors that wrap it.\n\n**Test, in `recovery_test.go`:** `TestPanicWithAbortHandler` checks that the status code the handler already set (204) is kept and the error message is logged without the full panic trace.\n\nThe change isn't committed. Your checkout is a detached HEAD, so if you want a commit I'll make a branch first and commit there with your title, `fix(recover): suppress http.ErrAbortHandler in recover`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":805,"cache_read_input_tokens":33350,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":805,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a9745105-e956-40da-ac59-8993cb062910","uuid":"d1453104-a758-450e-939e-3465a8a34bef","timestamp":"2026-10-18T15:39:27.716Z","request_id":"req_011Cg9xGNL657Hx9dbFyFew9"}
