ry.go`:** the check for whether a panic is a broken pipe now also matches `http.ErrAbortHandler`:\n```go\nif e, ok := err.(error); ok && errors.Is(e, http.ErrAbortHandler) {\n\tbrokenPipe = true\n}\n```\n`net/http` itself skips the stack trace for this value, because handlers raise it on purpose to abort a response. `errors.Is` also catches errors that wrap it.\n\n**Test, in `recovery_test.go`:** `TestPanicWithAbortHandler` checks that the status code the handler already set (204) is kept and the error message is logged without the full panic trace.\n\nThe change isn't committed. Your checkout is a detached HEAD, so if you want a commit I'll make a branch first and commit there with your title, `fix(recover): suppress http.ErrAbortHandler in recover`.","ttft_ms":1751,"type":"result","duration_ms":24097,"uuid":"f7116c23-7b4a-444b-8939-9056e2a0b173","ttft_stream_ms":1091,"time_to_request_ms":136,"first_content_frame_ms":1091,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
